      ],
      "text": "Test 1\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        50.04731369018555,
        59.533424377441406,
        126.78650665283203,
        69.35643005371094
      ],
      "text": "Questions 1-7\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.72020721435547,
        86.029052734375,
        459.15301513671875,
        97.81664276123047
      ],
      "text": "Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.39310073852539,
        111.87042999267578,
        248.99363708496094,
        122.34835815429688
      ],
      "text": "In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        86.02903747558594,
        137.71189880371094,
        366.1466369628906,
        172.721435546875
      ],
      "text": "TRUE\nif the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE\nif the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN\nif there is no information on this\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.39310073852539,
        196.59109497070312,
        457.29498291015625,
        217.86117553710938
      ],
      "text": "1\nPolar bears suffer from various health problems due to the build-up of fat under\ntheir skin.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        48.7388801574707,
        229.62884521484375,
        478.7990417480469,
        240.76158142089844
      ],
      "text": "2.\nThe study done by Liu and his colleagues compared different groups of polar bears.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.06599807739258,
        249.58233642578125,
        461.4002990722656,
        273.1445007324219
      ],
      "text": "3\nLiu and colleagues were the first researchers to compare polar bears and brown\nbears genetically.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        48.7388801574707,
        282.6201171875,
        461.2398986816406,
        293.7528381347656
      ],
      "text": "4\nPolar bears are able to control their levels of ‘bad’ cholesterol by genetic means.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.06599807739258,
        302.5736389160156,
        426.6451721191406,
        312.72406005859375
      ],
      "text": "5\nFemale polar bears are able to survive for about six months without food.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.06599807739258,
        322.5271301269531,
        473.1793518066406,
        346.08929443359375
      ],
      "text": "6\nIt was found that the bones of female polar bears were very weak when they came\nout of their dens in spring.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        48.73887634277344,
        354.2565002441406,
        455.2538757324219,
        378.7995910644531
      ],
      "text": "7 _ The polar bear’s mechanism for increasing bone density could also be used by\npeople one day.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        49.06596755981445,
        661.0824584960938,
        59.77871322631836,
        669.268310546875
      ],
      "text": "18\n"
    }
  ]
